              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "How many times do you need to write the fraction "
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\frac{1}{3}",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " to make this statement true?"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p111-q48-statement",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "align": "center",
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\frac{1}{3}\\div\\frac{1}{3}\\div\\frac{1}{3}\\div\\cdots\\div\\frac{1}{3}=81",
                "display": true
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "answerSpaceMm": 32,
      "answer": {
        "short": "6 terms.",
        "worked": "Replace each division after the first term with multiplication by its reciprocal. The first two terms give $\\frac13\\times3=1$. Since $81=3^4$, four further factors of $3$ are needed, giving $2+4=6$ terms.\n\nLet $n$ be the number of occurrences of $\\frac13$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac13\\times3^{n-1}&=81\\\\3^{n-2}&=3^4\\\\n-2&=4\\\\n&=6\\end{align*}$$",
        "provenance": {
          "short": "source",
          "worked": "source"
        }
      }
